A||||12||Fformula88||A few Clutch questions...||||5||
Z||000000||Fformula88||01-29-2001||10:38 PM||||I looked at an 85 SE V6 tonight with the 4 spd manual trans in it.  Since I know next to nothing about the Fiero manual transmissions I thought I'd post a couple general questions.<P>First, the owner of the car says that the clutch has to be pushed all the way down to shift gears.  Can the pedal or clutch be adjusted to shift sooner?  Or is it just how it is.  <P>Second, about how long do the clutches in Fiero's last milage wise?  This car has 69K miles on it now, but is in fairly mint condition.  There is absolutely no frame rust (and the trunk isn't rusted out either!!).  It looks like it was maintained well, so I am hoping the drivetrain was too.<P>Third, how hard is it to replace the clutch, and what are aproximate costs?  It probably isn't a job I would do myself unless it was fairly easy.  But I don't really have the facilities.  <P>Thanks for everybodies help.  Oh, and do you think this is a good deal?  Sounds like one to me.  As I said, it has 69K, power windows and locks, sunroof, V6 and 4 spd and no frame rust.  He's asking $2200 but immediately came down to $1900.  I think it sounds like a good deal anyway.  Thanks again!<P>------------------<BR>John<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/formula2m6/FIEROSIG1.JPG">     <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1987 Fiero Sport Coupe *In rebuilding*<BR>1997 Ford Probe SE<BR>AOL IM: Fformula88||||reg||5
Z||000001||AL||01-29-2001||11:05 PM||||first it seems the clutch pedal is bent,so you'll probably end up buying  a new steel one.2 it depends on how you treat it.3 i paid 900 for my 86gt now if you have the money buy it, it all depends on how bad you want it,good luck<B>AL</B>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/AL_sig.gif">  <BR>86gt 84 indy 89 gta 67olds cutlass<P>------------------<BR> <p>[This message has been edited by AL (edited 01-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fformula88||01-29-2001||11:51 PM||||Do the Fiero's have a problem with bent clutch pedals?  How do I tell if it is bent?  If thats its only problem it sounds like a really good fix.  <P>Sounds like you found a really good buy AL!  This is the first good Fiero that has an asking price close to what its worth that I have seen in my area in a while!  With all the road salt, the floorpans and frames rust thru after 13+ years of winters.  So I would definately pay more for a Fiero like this one that shows no rust underneath at all!<P>Thanks for the response.  Anyone else??||||reg||1
